      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Classes and Objects Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Class, Object, Reference",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Class== = blueprint; `new` builds an object on the ==heap==",
                "The variable holds a **reference**, not the object",
                "`b = a` copies the reference: both point to one object",
                "`==` compares **references**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "Dog a = new Dog(\"Rex\");",
                "Dog b = a;",
                "b.name = \"Max\";",
                "System.out.println(a.name);",
                "System.out.println(a == b);"
              ],
              "note": "one object, two references"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "Max",
                "true"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Defaults and this",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Default",
                "Unassigned use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Field",
                  "0, false, null",
                  "OK"
                ],
                [
                  "Local",
                  "none",
                  "{red:compile error}"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`this` = the ==current object==",
                "`this.name = name` resolves **name shadowing**",
                "`this(...)` chains to another constructor"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Common mistake",
              "text": "`==` on objects asks \"same reference?\", not \"same state?\". Use `equals` for state."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Class vs object?** Class is the blueprint; an object is one instance of it.",
                "**Where do objects live?** On the heap; variables hold references.",
                "**What does `==` compare?** References, not state.",
                "**Field vs local defaults?** Fields get 0, false, null; locals get none."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Constructors and Initialization Order",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Constructors and Initialization Order",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Constructor Rules",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Same name as the class, ==no return type==",
                "Write none: compiler adds a ==default no-arg== constructor",
                "Write any: default is ==gone==, `new Foo()` fails unless declared",
                "Explicit `super(...)`/`this(...)` first (Java 25 allows a prologue that does not touch `this`)",
                "Implicit `super()` fails if parent has no no-arg constructor"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Initialization Order",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "chain",
              "spec": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "text": "Static blocks",
                    "note": "once, at class load",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Parent fields + blocks",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Parent constructor",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Child fields + blocks",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Child constructor",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Overridable Call Bug",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Parent constructor calls overridable method: child override runs ==before child fields are set=="
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "class P { P() { show(); } void show() {} }",
                "class C extends P {",
                "  String s = \"hi\";",
                "  void show() { System.out.println(s); }",
                "}",
                "new C();"
              ],
              "note": "s is still null when show() runs"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "null"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Default constructor?** Only when you write none",
                "**Private constructor?** Yes: singleton, blocks outside `new`",
                "**Order?** Static, parent init, parent constructor, child init, child constructor",
                "**Inherited or overridden?** Neither"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Access Modifiers, static and final",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Access Modifiers, static and final",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Visibility, widest to narrowest",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Modifier",
                "Reach"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`public`",
                  "everywhere"
                ],
                [
                  "`protected`",
                  "same package + subclasses"
                ],
                [
                  "package-private",
                  "same package (no keyword)"
                ],
                [
                  "`private`",
                  "same class only"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. static and final",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`static` = ==class-level==: shared by all objects, used as `ClassName.member`",
                "A static method has no `this` and no direct instance fields",
                "`final` variable: ==assigned once==; a final reference can still have its object mutated",
                "`final` method: no override. `final` class: no extend (`String`)",
                "`static` methods are {red:hidden}, not overridden",
                "Constants: `public static final`, UPPER_CASE; a static block runs once at class load"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "final List<String> xs = new ArrayList<>();",
                "xs.add(\"a\");  // OK: object mutated",
                "xs = null;     // error: reassigned"
              ],
              "note": "final locks the reference"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**protected vs package-private?** protected also reaches subclasses in other packages",
                "**final means immutable?** No, only the reference is fixed",
                "**Override a static method?** No, it is hidden; the declared type decides",
                "**Why is String final?** Safe immutability: string pool, hash keys, security"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
