          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. extends and super",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`extends`: ==single== class inheritance",
                "`super.m()` calls the parent version",
                "`super(...)` calls the parent constructor (Java 25: a prologue not using this may precede)",
                "{red:private} members are not inherited"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Abstract class vs interface",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Abstract class",
                "Interface"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "State",
                  "fields allowed",
                  "constants only"
                ],
                [
                  "Constructors",
                  "yes",
                  "no"
                ],
                [
                  "Per class",
                  "extends one",
                  "implements many"
                ],
                [
                  "Methods",
                  "abstract + concrete",
                  "abstract; `default`, `static` (Java 8)"
                ],
                [
                  "Pick for",
                  "shared state, is-a family",
                  "capability, unrelated classes"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 4
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Abstract class ==cannot be instantiated=="
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Diamond problem",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "java",
              "lines": [
                "interface A { default void m() {} }",
                "interface B { default void m() {} }",
                "class C implements A, B {",
                "  public void m() { A.super.m(); }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "C must override m()"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Same default twice",
              "text": "Class **must override**; pick one with `A.super.m()`"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Abstract vs interface?** Shared state and code: abstract; capability: interface",
                "**Why one parent class?** Ambiguous state and constructors; interfaces carry none",
                "**Abstract constructor?** Yes, run via `super(...)`",
                "**Interface method body?** Yes: `default` or `static`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
